SUMMARY:The Hottest New Programming Language is Ubiquitous
DESCRIPTION:London Software Craftsmanship Community\nWe have a very specia
 l meetup for our November edition!\nWe are thrilled to welcome Hemal Varam
 bhia presenting:\n\n**The Hottest New Programming Language is Ubiquitous (
 Within a Bounded Context Window)**\n\n**Speaker Biography:**\nHemal Varamb
 hia is a senior technical coach at Simply Business\, an insurtech based in
  London. Prior to his career in software development\, he was an atomic\na
 nd molecular physicist at UCL\, in which he holds a doctorate. Outside of 
 software\ndevelopment\, Hemal enjoys reading and taking long walks and sti
 ll maintains a strong\ninterest in physics. Pronouns: He/Him/His\n\nKey Ta
 keaways:\n\n* This talk is a continuation of Hemal’s session at the LSCC
  in [September 2025](https://www.meetup.com/london-software-craftsmanship/
 events/310516638/?eventOrigin=group_events_list). Later that year\, he beg
 an to reap the benefits of DDD and Ports and Adapters: refining his progra
 mmer tests (no more Docker for unit tests!) and bringing the ubiquitous la
 nguage to life\, which made writing tests cheap and\, more importantly\, f
 un.\nTowards the end of 2025\, Hemal gave in to FOMO and started exploring
  AI-assisted programming. He was particularly interested in whether it was
  now possible to prompt an LLM entirely in the ubiquitous language and pro
 duce well-structured code\, and in what role refactoring plays when it doe
 s.\nIs the future of programming DDD’s ubiquitous language? Come along t
 o find out\, and see how **refactoring** can be unlocked as a superpower.\
 n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Food and Drinks**\nPizza and drinks will
  be provided upon arrival sponsored by [Codurance](https://www.codurance.c
 om/)\, with vegetarian and vegan options available.\n\nWe look forward to 
 seeing you!
